  "title": "Irish wildfires",
  "dek": "Wildfires across Europe were once outliers but there is now a pattern and extreme fires have been a regular feature in Europe's summers since 2021. Ireland will not be immune to them.",
  "eyebrow": "Series | Research Matters",
  "abstract": "Wildfires devastated Europe in 2026, including several large fires in Ireland. Land management and habitat restoration provides protection against wildfire. Policy encouraging habitat restoration can create a \"win-win-win\" situation by mitigating fires, managing water and reducing carbon emissions.",
  "topics": [
